webrtc-sdk/webrtc's m150_release (2a0b277: its m150 commit 89d790b and the 17 after it) moved
to branch-head 8078, for the macOS framework only: the Objective-C SDK the plugin's macOS
code is written against (the audio engine device module, desktop capture, audio
processing, YUV helper, simulcast factory...) and the C++ it needs. Left out: Android,
its README and TESTING notes, the webrtc-sdk/build fork (tvOS and visionOS only), and its
revert of goog_cc's probe controller; and what Fogata never uses: the frame and data
packet cryptor (end-to-end frame encryption), H.265, its changes to the VideoToolbox H.264
encoder and decoder (0004 leaves VideoToolbox out of the framework), and its OpenGL view
for macOS. Where M156 changed what the commit changed, M156's design is kept: global audio
options applied when a source is made (not per channel), the teardown of stopped
transceivers, the media engine reference count.
